# The answer key to tool-call-probe.txt: line N is the tool prompt N needs, in
# the same order, comments and blank lines skipped on both sides.
#
# It is here for the reason map-order-probe.key is: a corpus whose key is not on
# disk can only be scored by hand. What it adds to the four shapes is the one
# result a shape cannot carry — *the format held and the model called the wrong
# thing* — which is the failure a grammar would make more likely rather than
# less, because a grammar constrains the form and never the choice.
#
# A prompt answerable by two tools is not in the corpus. "What is in this
# directory" is `list_dir` and not `run_command ls`, even though the policy
# allows `ls`, because a key that admits two answers cannot score the third.

read_file
list_dir
read_file
run_command
list_dir
read_file
run_command
read_file
list_dir
read_file
